# Scroll entrance for every new visual

Every new visual component or chart added to this site must include a bespoke, choreographed scroll-triggered entrance:

- Staggered reveal as the scene enters, then a smooth fade-in.
- Smooth fade-out when the scene leaves, in both scroll directions.
- Do not use `pin: true` or any other pin that traps scroll height.
- Upward and downward scrolling must stay smooth, including a return to the top of the page.
- When `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set, show the finished visual immediately with no motion.

Existing charts, published data files, and the dark midnight theme stay as they are unless the task asks to change them.
